<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Code coverage scope for the FXPA baseline suite.

  This file is applied AUTOMATICALLY to every test run: the test project
  points at it with the RunSettingsFilePath property, so no extra switch
  is needed and the scope cannot be forgotten.

  To measure coverage, run the tests with the collect switch and the
  friendly name "XPlat Code Coverage" (the README has the full command
  line).

  The measurement covers the application's own code only:

  * GENERATED code is excluded - the WinForms designer output, the
    settings and resource designers, and the assembly attributes. None of
    it is hand written logic; the tooling regenerates it and no test can
    meaningfully cover it.

  * VENDORED third-party components are excluded - code that arrived from
    elsewhere and is not ours to cover. QuickenToolStrip, TitleStrip and
    HeaderRenderer declare namespaces of the .NET framework and of its
    Samples tree; DOATransparentLabel, ManagedTreeView, DSWebClient and
    ThreadPoolEx are vendor components that kept their product names, and
    the application only calls them.

  The .NET framework itself and the NuGet packages are never instrumented
  by coverlet in the first place, so they need no entry here. The TA-Lib
  binary is a pre-built DLL with no source; it is not instrumented either.

  Notes for whoever edits this file:
   - the pattern lists are COMMA separated; a semicolon list is read as one
     single pattern that never matches anything;
   - the pattern shape needs a wildcard segment - **/*Name.cs works, while
     a literal **/dir/Name.cs does not;
   - SourceLink is off because it rewrites the reported file names into
     raw.githubusercontent.com URLs, which breaks path based exclusions.

  After changing the exclusions, re-measure and update the number in
  README.md - the recorded coverage figure must describe the same set of
  files the report contains.
-->
<RunSettings>
  <DataCollectionRunSettings>
    <DataCollectors>
      <DataCollector friendlyName="XPlat code coverage">
        <Configuration>
          <Format>cobertura</Format>
          <ExcludeByFile>**/*.designer.cs,**/*.Designer.cs,**/Properties/AssemblyInfo.cs,**/Properties/Resources.Designer.cs,**/Properties/Settings.Designer.cs,**/*QuickenToolStrip.cs,**/*TitleStrip.cs,**/*HeaderRenderer.cs,**/*DOATransparentLabel.cs,**/*ManagedTreeView.cs,**/*DSWebClient.cs,**/*ThreadPoolEx.cs</ExcludeByFile>
          <ExcludeByAttribute>Obsolete,GeneratedCodeAttribute,CompilerGeneratedAttribute</ExcludeByAttribute>
          <IncludeTestAssembly>false</IncludeTestAssembly>
          <SingleHit>false</SingleHit>
          <UseSourceLink>false</UseSourceLink>
          <SkipAutoProps>true</SkipAutoProps>
        </Configuration>
      </DataCollector>
    </DataCollectors>
  </DataCollectionRunSettings>
</RunSettings>
